  "scope": "Input-only retail USA C4 and Ninja optical camouflage scenario review. PSX reference is the native runtime framebuffer, not a new donor execution. No full-game or complete-scene certification.",
  "previous_spatial_work": "docs/mgs-effects-v14-evidence.json",
  "changes": [
    "Read-only actor_<basename>_count predicates traverse all nine USA GV lists. Unknown or malformed lists never mean zero; unlinked stale allocations cannot satisfy a goal.",
    "Adaptive recording completion is based on explicit route success. A completed route can finish before its frame safety budget; fixed-length recordings still cannot end early, and failed/missing routes fail.",
    "Fixed a real Vulkan exception in the Ninja cinematic: a source KMD face with authenticated kogaku2 Direct15 scene sampling is declared as a runtime material before submission. The strict recorder remains unchanged; ordinary missing materials are not accepted.",
    "Ninja native reveal thresholds and thermal exclusion retain ordinary materials on unaffected faces. No scene-wide color guess activates camouflage.",
    "Restored the broad horizontal lens response of EQ_VisibleUnit2 (quarter contraction around the view centre), evaluated continuously inside the original animated mesh with the modern scene color and source normals. Tiny normal offsets alone made the original silhouette illegible."
  ],
